    "last_assistant_text": "The PoC successfully triggered the vulnerability. The ASAN output confirms:\n- `heap-buffer-overflow on address 0x502000000114` at `read.hpp:543` — exactly the `memcpy(&c, it, 5)` in the bool parser\n- `READ of size 5` — matches \"Container-overflow READ 5\"\n- The 6-byte region `[0x502000000110,0x502000000116)` is the buffer `['t','r','u','\\0']` (4 bytes) which was allocated as 6 bytes (vector with push_back reallocation)\n- The read at `0x502000000114` is 4 bytes into the 6-byte allocation, reading 5 bytes would go to `0x502000000119`, past the end at `0x502000000116`\n\nThe PoC is just the 3 bytes `tru`. When the fuzz target appends `\\0` and passes it through `read_json` with a const reference (no padding), the bool parser's bounds check (`end - it < 4`) passes with 4 bytes remaining, but then unconditionally reads 5 bytes via `memcpy(&c, it, 5)`.",
